.TH SSO\-MIB\-GCH\-SMTP\-O365 1 "2025" "@PACKAGE_NAME@ @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365 \- git credential helper for Office 365 SMTP using Microsoft Identity Broker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365
.RI [ client_id ]
.RI [ authority ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365
is a git credential helper that authenticates
.BR git\-send\-email (1)
on Office 365 using OAuth2 tokens obtained from the Microsoft Identity Broker
via the sso-mib library.
.PP
It acquires an access token for the
.I https://outlook.office365.com/SMTP.Send
scope and outputs credentials in the format expected by
.BR git\-credential (1).
.PP
The helper only responds to the
.B get
command for the
.B smtp
protocol. The
.BR approve ,
.BR reject ,
and
.B capability
commands are silently ignored.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I client_id
Azure client application ID. Can also be set via the environment variable
.BR MIB_GCH_SMTP_CLIENT_ID .
The command-line argument takes precedence.
.TP
.I authority
Entra ID (Azure AD) authority URL (e.g.\&
.IR https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant_id> ).
Can also be set via the environment variable
.BR MIB_GCH_SMTP_AUTHORITY .
The command-line argument takes precedence.
.TP
.I command
The git credential helper command. One of
.BR get ,
.BR approve ,
.BR reject ,
or
.BR capability .
Only
.B get
produces output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MIB_GCH_SMTP_CLIENT_ID
Azure client application ID. Used when no
.I client_id
argument is provided on the command line.
.TP
.B MIB_GCH_SMTP_AUTHORITY
Entra ID authority URL. Used when no
.I authority
argument is provided on the command line.
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=ssomib
Enable debug logging of DBus call parameters via GLib's message logging system.
.SH GIT CONFIGURATION
Add the following to your
.B .gitconfig
to use this helper for SMTP credentials:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[credential "smtp://"]
    helper = !sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365 <client_id> <authority>
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or, using environment variables:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[credential "smtp://"]
    helper = !sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT
On a successful
.B get
command for the
.B smtp
protocol, the helper outputs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
username=<user@example.com>
password=<access_token>
password_expiry_utc=<epoch_seconds>
authtype=bearer
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a non-applicable command/protocol was received.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (e.g., missing authority or client ID, broker communication
failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
Use with git send-email:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ git config \-\-global credential.smtp://.helper \\
    \(aq!sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365 <client_id> https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant_id>\(aq
$ git send\-email \-\-smtp\-auth=xoauth2 *.patch
.fi
.RE
.PP
Test the helper manually:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ echo "protocol=smtp" | sso\-mib\-gch\-smtp\-o365 <client_id> <authority> get
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sso\-mib\-tool (1),
.BR git\-credential (1),
.BR git\-send\-email (1)
.SH AUTHORS
@PACKAGE_AUTHORS@
